{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuoKcthiMLvkDnpF9bw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS with 17 tests passing (5 existing shipment tests + 4 new confirm tests + 4 order tests + 3 customer tests + 1 application test)\n\n**Failures:** None\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ \"Existing build passes\" — All 17 tests pass, including 4 existing OrderControllerTest, 3 existing CustomerControllerTest, 1 existing SampleServiceApplicationTests, and 5 existing ShipmentControllerTest.\n\n2. ✅ \"Existing tests pass\" — 5 existing ShipmentControllerTest cases pass unchanged.\n\n3. ✅ \"`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it\" — New test `confirms a created shipment and transitions to confirmed status` verifies: creates S-4 in CREATED, POSTs to /shipments/S-4/confirm, expects 200 OK with shipment.status = CONFIRMED. Controller logic: fetches shipment, checks status is not CANCELLED, copies with status=CONFIRMED, saves to repository, returns OK.\n\n4. ✅ \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" — Uses ConflictException (409) for CANCELLED state (consistent with ShipmentController.create() line 29-32 for duplicates), ResourceNotFoundException (404) for missing shipment (consistent with ShipmentController.getById() line 48-52). Both throw standard ApiException subclasses caught by GlobalExceptionHandler, producing ApiError envelope with ErrorCode.\n\n5. ✅ \"A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused\" — Three dedicated tests:\n   - `confirming an already confirmed shipment is idempotent`: Creates S-5 in CREATED, confirms once (200 OK), confirms again (200 OK, shipment unchanged). Verifies no-op save on retry.\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with conflict error`: Manually sets S-6 to CANCELLED, POSTs confirm, expects 409 Conflict with code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE.\n   - `rejects confirming a nonexistent shipment with not found error`: POSTs confirm with id \"S-missing\", expects 404 Not Found with code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND.\n\n6. ✅ \"No new Maven dependency appears\" — Only Kotlin code edited. No pom.xml changes, no new imports of external libraries.\n\n7. ✅ \"No unrelated production file changes\" — Only three files modified:\n   - ApiError.kt: added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE enum value (required for error code)\n   - ShipmentController.kt: added confirm() method (required for endpoint)\n   - ShipmentControllerTest.kt: added four test cases (required for verification)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **ApiError.kt** (required) — Added one line to ErrorCode enum: `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE,`. Necessary because the requirement specifies 409 response for CANCELLED shipment, and the enum is the API contract.\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt** (required) — Added confirm method with @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\"), fetching shipment, checking status, transitioning if CREATED, saving, returning 200 OK. Necessary because this is the entire feature.\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (required) — Added four test cases covering: happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED), idempotency (retry CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED), forbidden state (CANCELLED→error), missing resource (not found). Necessary for verification and acceptance criteria.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All four use cases named in the requirement have implementation and test coverage.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint; CREATED→CONFIRMED transitions with idempotent retries; CANCELLED and unknown shipment IDs rejected with 409 and 404.\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt — added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE to ErrorCode enum\n              ShipmentController.kt — added confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId) method\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added fo